The mapping of flash sectors for star platforms goes like this:
/dev/mtdblock1: BOOT loader, offset 0, size 128K
/dev/mtdblock2: Linux Kernel and fs compressed, offset 256K
/dev/mtdblock3: Non-volatile and boot params, offset 128K, size 64K
/dev/mtdblock4: FS2, volatile params, offset and size are defined by config_offset boot parameter and the WINDOW_SIZE
